# Keep Windows batch scripts and scripting hosts on CRLF in the repository
# itself, not only on checkout.
#
# Why "-text" rather than "text eol=crlf":
#   "text eol=crlf" only converts on checkout, so the blob stays LF. Anything
#   that consumes the blob directly - "Download ZIP", `git archive` - still
#   yields a broken file.
#   "-text" tells git to store the file verbatim, so the CRLF committed here is
#   what everyone gets, no matter how they obtain the repository.
#
# Why CRLF matters here:
#   cmd.exe looks for CRLF to find line boundaries. With bare LF it splits lines
#   mid-token, e.g. `chcp 65001` becomes `chcp 6` + `01`, producing
#   '01' is not recognized as an internal or external command.
#   This stays hidden on machines with core.autocrlf=true, which is exactly why
#   it needs to be declared rather than left to each machine's config.
*.cmd  -text
*.bat  -text
*.ps1  -text
*.psm1 -text
*.vbs  -text
